# EclipseOS Phase 1 desktop stack.
#
# X11 plus lightdm and openbox: the smallest honest graphical session that
# proves the display stack on UEFI and BIOS. Phase 2 replaces lightdm/openbox
# with the full Plasma session; nothing here is on the Phase 2 critical path
# except the X server, fonts and the X11 video drivers.
#
# Every package is from Debian main (docs/licenses.md).

# Display manager and greeter
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter

# X server, input and video drivers.
# xserver-xorg-core provides the modesetting driver used by real hardware and
# by QEMU (bochs-drm/ virtio). The vesa/fbdev/vmware drivers cover VirtualBox
# (VMSVGA exposes a VMware SVGA II device) and firmware fallbacks.
# xserver-xorg-legacy keeps X startable on consoles that do not have a logind
# seat (and is the standard Debian desktop configuration).
xserver-xorg-core
xserver-xorg-legacy
xserver-xorg-input-libinput
xserver-xorg-video-vesa
xserver-xorg-video-fbdev
xserver-xorg-video-vmware
xinit
xauth
x11-utils
x11-xserver-utils

# Boot splash. The script plugin lives in the main plymouth package; the
# EclipseOS theme is shipped in includes.chroot, so plymouth-themes is not
# installed (no Debian theme artwork ends up in the image).
plymouth

# Session and shell
openbox
xterm
feh
fastfetch

# Fonts, icons, cursors
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-liberation
fonts-inter
adwaita-icon-theme
hicolor-icon-theme
